# Repo-root build context for conductor/Dockerfile (it needs the sibling packages
# harness/ + provisioner/, so its context is the repo root — see that Dockerfile's
# header). Keep the context (and image) free of local state and — load-bearing — of
# secrets: any package's .env holds OPENROUTER_API_KEY on a dev box and must never
# enter the image. Only the paths the Dockerfile COPYs (pyproject/uv.lock/README/src)
# survive; everything below is stripped.
**/.env
**/.venv
**/.python-version
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/node_modules
**/dist
conductor/runs
# Docs, CI, git, and other trees the image never needs.
.git
.github
docs
scripts
k8s
# deploy/ is excluded EXCEPT the per-engagement Helm chart, which the control-plane
# fat image bakes in for the conductor's --k8s path (control-plane/Dockerfile ships
# it at /app/engagement-chart). Exclude-then-negate level by level so the chart
# survives the context strip on every builder (not just BuildKit).
deploy/*
!deploy/helm
deploy/helm/*
!deploy/helm/engagement
